--- body ---
## Context

Author, 2026-09-06: wants essential technical details hidden by default
but discoverable in the plugin's own window -- not removed, not exiled to
a log file only. Ticket 0686 already asked to "move technical diagnostics
below primary progress information." The dialog already has the right
skeleton: two existing `<details>` disclosures (`sdt-details`,
`sdt-index-details`).

## Design: three layers

1. **Primary** (always visible): progress bar, "Index 43 %" (0691),
   current document title, elapsed time, estimated finish, p5/p50/p95
   labelled "total scenarios" per SPEC.md R22.
2. **Details** (`<details>`, closed by default): observation count,
   covariate used (per-page vs. per-byte), last exceptions in plain
   words, native text-search-index stats (0691's renamed Zotero panel).
3. **Diagnostics** (`<details>` nested inside Details, closed by
   default): the debug checkbox from 0689, the ring-buffer tail (last 50
   records, auto-refreshed), a "copy journal" action, versions (plugin,
   Zotero, pack/schema/processor), admission readings, install path.

Nothing already shown is removed -- this is ordering, not deletion. 0689
has merged, so this is one build pass, not two: the debug checkbox and
ring-buffer tail (`Zotero.SDTPackSitter.journal.tail(50)`, already wired)
land in the same pass as the rest of the diagnostics layer.

## Acceptance

- [x] Diagnostics disclosure hosts a debug checkbox (new UI, bound to the existing `extensions.sdt-pack-sitter.debug` pref) and ring tail;
      opening the disclosure does not require debug mode
      to already be on.
- [ ] 0686's still-open accessibility items (keyboard open/focus/close/
      Escape/focus-return, reduced-motion, transition-only announcements)
      are verified in a real window against the reorganized layout, not
      re-approved from the old one -- verified once, after 0689's wiring
      lands, not twice.

      NOT MET by this branch, and it cannot be: a real window needs a Zotero
      run, which no headless lane has. What the branch does instead is make
      the verification executable — `verification/probes/sdt-sitter-harness/`
      now asserts the layer structure, the nesting, closed-by-default, the
      bound label, focus on each summary, and a ring tail readable with the
      debug pref off, and it records the reduced-motion reading and the
      toolbar's accessible name rather than leaving them to another reading
      of the source. The remaining items (Escape, focus return, reduced-motion
      behaviour, transition-only announcements) are 0686's own open scope and
      0686 stays open for them; this ticket's criterion pointed at 0686
      rather than duplicating it.
